# Supabase project this app syncs to. Both values are safe in a client bundle: the URL identifies the
# project, and the publishable/anon key only says "an anonymous visitor of this project" - what
# actually grants access is row-level security (see supabase/schema.sql).
#
# Supabase renamed this key: new projects show a publishable key (sb_publishable_...) in
# Connect -> Framework, older ones an anon JWT. Set whichever your project gives you; the app accepts
# either, and the publishable one wins if both are set.
#
# NEVER put the secret key (service_role) here, or in any other VITE_ variable: everything prefixed
# VITE_ is compiled into the JavaScript every visitor downloads.
#
# Leave these unset to run the app entirely locally - that is a supported mode, not a degraded one:
# nothing syncs, everything still works.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Older projects only:
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
